    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="be-overview">
      <h2 class="t-h4" id="be-overview" data-i18n="ovTitle">01 · Overview</h2>
      <div class="chapter-body pair">
        <div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ovProbT">The problem</h3>
          <p data-i18n="beProb">
            Best Egg helps people in the US pay off and consolidate personal loans. In 2024 it had 1.5 million
            active users on its web platform and no mobile app, so everything they needed to manage their loans
            lived on the website.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ovGoalT">The goal</h3>
          <p data-i18n="beGoal">
            Design the first version of a native iOS and Android app that brings the core account tasks to mobile,
            while meeting every legal and compliance requirement a lending product carries.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="be-constraints">
      <h2 class="t-h4" id="be-constraints" data-i18n="beConTitle">02 · Constraints</h2>
      <div class="chapter-body quote">
        <p class="quote-lead" data-i18n="beQuote">
          An app is more than the website copied onto a smaller screen: it has to meet the expectations of its
          platform.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="insights two">
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="beC1t">Web first</p>
          <p data-i18n="beC1">
            The app had to inherit the information architecture of Best Egg’s web platform, adapted to a smaller
            screen, and still feel like a tool of its own, built for what mobile users need.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="beC2t">Legal on every screen</p>
          <p data-i18n="beC2">
            Screens were tied to required legal copy and had to go through multiple bank compliance and legal
            sign-offs.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

